# Orchestrator-ready plans

Any `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md` produced during planning MUST carry per-workstream orchestration
metadata so the `orchestrate-epic` skill can execute it without manual triage.

Before finishing a plan, read `.cursor/skills/orchestrate-epic/plan-template.md` and ensure every
todo in the frontmatter has:

- `phase` — integer execution batch (a human reviews at each phase boundary)
- `run_as` — `subagent` (no parent-held gate) or `parent` (the orchestrator routes the human gate,
  presents it to the user, and relays the approved context); a fresh subagent always performs the work
- `model_role` — a valid role, never a model version (omit only to let the orchestrator infer from task type)
- `exit_gates` — list of gates that must pass before the workstream is marked complete
- `heavy` — optional `true`; set it on any workstream whose sub-steps emit large tool output
  (native builds, CI logs, screenshots, long test runs) so the orchestrator offloads that noise to
  the subagent performing the work while the parent retains the human gate.
  `run_as` decides who routes the gate; `heavy` decides who absorbs the tokens.

Also include the phases-summary table (with a Role column) as shown in the template, and for each
phase in the body: **Run as**, **Inputs** (exact files the executing agent must read), **Exit** gates.

Rules:

- Protected-file edits (see `.cursorrules` §1.5), ADR acceptance, and PR creation use
  `run_as: parent` for the user gate; after the user approves, the orchestrator relays that approval
  in the dispatch prompt and a subagent performs the work.
- Valid `model_role` values: `BUILDER`, `ARCHITECT`, `SCRIBE`, `DEEP`, `OPERATOR`, `BULK`.
  **Never write a model name or version into a plan** — model lineups turn over every few weeks and
  pinned slugs go stale silently. The orchestrator resolves the role to a live slug at dispatch time.
  Role definitions, family ladders, and the resolution procedure live in `docs/MODEL_ROUTING.md`,
  which is the single source of truth; do not restate them in a plan. An optional `model` field
  exists to pin one specific slug, but it needs a stated reason.
- Workstreams are numbered `<phase>.<ordinal>`; the ordinal resets to 1 in each phase. Todo IDs
  follow `e{epic}-ws{phase}.{ordinal}-{shortname}`.
- Cursor's Plan mode may write the plan **outside the repository** and may **strip custom frontmatter
  fields**. Before handing off to the orchestrator: copy the plan into `.cursor/plans/`, re-check that
  every todo still carries the fields above, and backfill any that were dropped.
- This extends `.cursorrules` §1.3 / §1.3.1 — it does not replace them. Keep the standard plan
  structure and add the metadata the orchestrator consumes on top.
